Chapter: EqPlainSum

 A sum that derives NOTHING and names its own type in no field. Before
 COMPILER-63 the desugarer built `__eq_<T>` only for a sum deriving `Eq` or
 naming itself in a field, so a sum of this shape reached every backend with no
 helper and each backend needed an inline equality of its own. The arm64 one
 refuses two shapes rather than guess, and `Pair` below is the first of them:
 more than one field-carrying constructor, where two constructors hold
 different types at the same field index.

 `Holder` is the second refused shape: a field that RESOLVES TO A SUM. Inlining
 that comparison does not terminate on a recursive type, so the helper is what
 makes the field compare by calling the field type's own equality.

Section: Definitions

  Pair =
    | Both (Integer) (Integer)
    | JustText (Text)
    | Neither

  Holder =
    | Wraps (Pair)
    | Empty

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (if Both 1 2 == Both 1 2 then "both eq : yes" else "both eq : no")
    print-line-uni (if Both 1 2 == Both 1 3 then "both ne : no" else "both ne : yes")
    print-line-uni (if JustText "a" == JustText "a" then "text eq : yes" else "text eq : no")
    print-line-uni (if Both 1 2 == Neither then "cross ne : no" else "cross ne : yes")
    print-line-uni (if Wraps (Both 1 2) == Wraps (Both 1 2) then "sum field eq : yes" else "sum field eq : no")
    print-line-uni (if Wraps (Both 1 2) == Wraps (JustText "a") then "sum field ne : no" else "sum field ne : yes")
  end

